{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9tmfTVUZ64uyiovBMP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VVdCMfezf71RP7zdMSnQ2B","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-982\\docs\\reviews\\wi-982\\004-ADJUDICATE-f8f3572.md","content":"Adjudicated: f8f357217\n\n## amendment\n\nJudged on the cells as shown: LLR-360 `Detail` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:8033a9d838b2d493) and TC-399 `Expected` and `Method` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:0ed55ebbe86913e9). The anchor is the 880ad86e1 copy. This re-sits both rows after `003-ADJUDICATE-9973897.md`. Since then, LLR-360's two added sentences were narrowed (D-006). TC-399's cells are byte-identical to the text that sitting blessed: same JUDGED-TEXT identity. The rung is released. To decide whether to bless, I read the new text against the WI-982 Done-when, the mint's authoring-tags writer and its two drafters, and the hat reader.\n\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-360 Detail -> before: a decomposition round widens each parent need by \"the authoring work item's declared tags\", and says nothing about where a minted row's tags come from, so a minted row widens by its own Workstream and SafetyClass -> after: a first-approval or amendment row that a route mints RECORDS the declared tags of the work items the route names as its authors, and those tags REPLACE the row's own classification; a route naming no author records none, and the row widens by its own tags; such a row minted from a minted row passes the record on; and the minted and in-lane sittings for one SR reach one perspective set wherever the author is named -> not the same. A correct build of the old text, where a minted adjudication row widens by `process`/`adjudication`, fails the new text, which adds a recording duty, a replacement rule, a pass-on rule and a cross-route equality. I would bless the new text. Sitting 003's finding is answered: the duty is now scoped to the two row kinds the build writes the cell on, the only writers, with a `## Dispositions` draft refused the key. It is also scoped to \"a route\" rather than \"the merge\", so the `sweep --merged ... --branch` route is in. \"Such a row\" closes the pass-on sentence's twin of the same over-reach (D-006). The pass-on reads true against the build: the minted row records its author's cell when the author has one (`test_a_minted_author_passes_its_cell_on`), and otherwise the author's own tags. Every clause binds to an existing TC-399 evidence node through the coordinator's arms map. The row names no implementation carrier, carries no `shall`, and leaves every approved sentence byte-exact. It adds detail under the same SR-161 decision, so it keeps its id under §4 \"Keep or mint\".\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-399 Expected, Method -> before: verify the round/non-round states, needs as parents, tag widening without sibling merge, the roster cases, the template slot, the combined sitting and non-ruling outcome lines -> after: the same states plus four: a minted row's recorded authoring tags stand in place of its own; a row minted from a minted row passes them on; the minted and in-lane rows for one SR compose one hat set; and a route naming no authoring work item leaves the row widening by its own tags. Expected now requires one perspective set across the two routes wherever the author is named -> not the same, because the TC now obliges four more checks and one more expected outcome. I would bless it, as sitting 003 did on this identical text. Each new clause names a state its evidence drives. The method's \"a minted row's recorded authoring tags\" and \"passes them on\" describe a minted row that carries a record, which under the narrowed LLR is a first-approval or amendment row, so they claim nothing the build lacks. The text needs no change to agree with the narrowed parent.\n\nThe rung is released, so neither row is held for the owner and no CLARITY row waits on either one. The later act re-attests both LLR-360 and TC-399.\n\nVERDICT: MEANING rows=2\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1819,"cache_read_input_tokens":214542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1819},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c376c8c-200c-488f-950a-1fb2b7b7f425","uuid":"e2b6e6e8-5a46-4458-9007-f53f9e8110f8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:31:39.348Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9tmXmkBuknk7hBtq3C","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VVdCMfezf71RP7zdMSnQ2B":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-982\\docs\\reviews\\wi-982\\004-ADJUDICATE-f8f3572.md","content":"Adjudicated: f8f357217\n\n## amendment\n\nJudged on the cells as shown: LLR-360 `Detail` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:8033a9d838b2d493) and TC-399 `Expected` and `Method` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:0ed55ebbe86913e9). The anchor is the 880ad86e1 copy. This re-sits both rows after `003-ADJUDICATE-9973897.md`. Since then, LLR-360's two added sentences were narrowed (D-006). TC-399's cells are byte-identical to the text that sitting blessed: same JUDGED-TEXT identity. The rung is released. To decide whether to bless, I read the new text against the WI-982 Done-when, the mint's authoring-tags writer and its two drafters, and the hat reader.\n\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-360 Detail -> before: a decomposition round widens each parent need by \"the authoring work item's declared tags\", and says nothing about where a minted row's tags come from, so a minted row widens by its own Workstream and SafetyClass -> after: a first-approval or amendment row that a route mints RECORDS the declared tags of the work items the route names as its authors, and those tags REPLACE the row's own classification; a route naming no